@startuml UC1_Login_SignUp_Activity_Diagram

title UC1: Login / Sign Up - Activity Diagram

start
:User opens the application\nor navigates to any page;
:Frontend's Firebase SDK restores any
existing session from local persistence;

note right
  Route guard - this check runs on
  every page, not just app launch.
  Any page other than the login form
  requires a valid session; a session
  that expires mid-use re-triggers
  this same check (Alternative Flow A4).
end note

if (Session restored?) then (yes)
else (no)
  :Frontend displays its own login form;

  if (User selects "Register"?) then (yes)
    :Frontend calls Firebase Client SDK
    to create account (username, email,
    password) on Authentication Service;
    note right: Alternative Flow A1 - New Account
  else (no)
  endif

  if (User selects "Forgot Password"?) then (yes)
    :Frontend calls Firebase Client SDK's
    password-reset flow;
    note right: Alternative Flow A3 - Forgot Password
    stop
  endif

  :User enters credentials into
  Frontend's form;

  if (Authentication Service available?) then (no)
    :Frontend displays maintenance message;
    note right: Exception E1 - Authentication Service unavailable
    stop
  endif

  :Frontend calls Firebase Client SDK
  to sign in;

  if (Credentials valid?) then (no)
    :Firebase Client SDK returns error;
    :Frontend displays it and re-prompts;
    note right: Alternative Flow A2 - Invalid Credentials
    stop
  endif

  :Authentication Service issues
  Firebase ID token to the Frontend;
endif

:Frontend holds a valid Firebase ID
token and an active session;

note right
  Continues into Create Profile (UC2)
  on the Frontend's first authenticated
  call to the User Actions Server
end note

stop

@enduml
